.TH OMACHAT-PROTOCOL 7 "2026-08-31" "OmaChat 0.0.1"
.SH NAME
omachat-protocol \- OmaChat compatibility and IPC contract
.SH DESCRIPTION
IPC v2 is newline-delimited JSON over a 0600 Unix socket. Clients must begin
with hello and a supported version range. Lines are limited to 65536 bytes;
unknown fields and unsupported versions are rejected.
Responses retain request IDs.
.PP
Wire behavior targets the immutable upstream pins documented in
docs/compatibility-profile.md. A codec passing hermetic tests is not a live
interoperability claim. Courier v1 and v2, Android limitations, bridge health,
and uncompleted hardware/live gates are documented there and in SECURITY.md.

.SH SUBSCRIPTIONS
Subscribe returns a bounded recent-message snapshot and current status.
Streamed events are filtered by the requested topics and interleaved with
correlated responses. Clients must deduplicate snapshot/live overlap by message ID.
Destructive commands require a daemon-issued, single-use token, valid for 120 seconds.
